  "scope_disclaimer": "Standalone reproducibility archive of the closed single-tree lazy integer (x in {0,1}^n) linked Benders diagnostic on adapted public Diaz instances (p26, p50) using open-source OR-Tools 9.15.6755 (GSCIP, solve_calls == 1) + SciPy HiGHS dual-simplex callbacks. Preserves the p26 3-arm pilot pass (17 vs. 26 vs. 43 sweeps, 9.70 s vs. 15.55 s vs. 24.16 s; including orig_multi_floor's 1 tiny unseparated callback discrepancy of 1.09127e-05 matching max_subproblem_duality_err) and the p50 4-arm formal closure (5 vs. 5 sweeps against matched single-cut control A3 orig_single_hinge_floor, 5.04 s vs. 5.42 s vs. 6.25 s vs. 6.59 s, shared exact-optimal mechanical cold seed, lightly sampled 5-6 layout regime). Because p26 did not include A3, p50 blocks generalization/attribution of price separation without identifying what caused the p26 speedup. Not a journal submission or general advantage claim. Smoke artifacts, raw matrices, adapted p*.json inputs, prompts, logs, and PDFs are excluded.",
